  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nA front, currently draped across southern WV and northeast KY, will \nbegin to shift north as a warm front while the parent low tracks \ntowards the Great Lakes Region. Showers are expected to continue in\nthe vicinity of the front today, then activity will diminish as\nthe front exits the area this evening into tonight.\n\nA marginal risk of excessive rainfall remains present across \nportions of central and southern West Virginia, northeast Kentucky, \nand southwest Virginia, where heavier downpours could prompt \nisolated high water issues. While isolated storms are not \nentirely out of the question along the boundary later this \nafternoon, the risk of severe weather remains low for today.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nA low pressure system and upper trough will usher a strong cold \nfront across the area on Friday, with showers, storms, and gusty \nwinds expected to occur during the frontal passage. Precipitation \nshould then persist through the night as the upper trough passes \noverhead. Blustery conditions will also continue into Saturday \nmorning, with 25-30 mph gusts expected across the lowlands, and up \nto 45 mph gusts possible along the higher terrain.\n\nCold air advection will quickly lower temperatures from west to east \nbehind the front, likely sending temperatures into the 50s across \nmuch of the area by the end of the day. Temperatures further lower \ninto the 30s to 40s overnight, which may allow some snowflakes to \nmaterialize over the higher elevations of the northeast mountains \nearly Saturday morning. Snow accumulations are not anticipated.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3...\n\nOn Saturday, winds gradually relax and precipitation comes to an end \nas high pressure builds in from the west during the day. Northerly \nflow will keep temperatures below normal, with highs likely \nremaining in the 50s in the lowlands and 30s to 40s in the \nmountains. Under calm winds and clear skies, overnight lows are \nexpected to plummet into the 20s to 30s, resulting frost and freeze \nconditions across the entirety of the forecast area late Saturday \nnight into early Sunday morning.\n\nDry conditions are generally expected to continue into the new work \nweek, though temperatures trend warmer as high pressure meanders \ntowards the east coast.",
